    "url": "https://www.biotic.org/",
    "finalUrl": "https://biotic.org/",
    "status": 200,
    "title": "Biotic | Biology is Open Technology Inspiring Civilization",
    "text": "Like most websites, we use cookies to improve your browsing experience, understand site traffic, and personalize content. Learn more in our Privacy Policy\n\nManage\nReject\nAccept\nAbout\nResearch\nCommunity\nNews\nFAQ\nContact\nContact\nOut\nof\none,\nmany.\n(Ex uno plures)\n\nWe have limited time to unlock unlimited resources. By 2050, humanity is expected to consume natural resources faster than Earth can regenerate them. Biotic is developing technologies that enable people and nations to produce essential resources locally, sustainably, and independently, creating a more resilient future.\n\nDays left to 2050\n8485\nDays\n13\nHours\n18\nMinutes\n34\nSeconds\nAbout us\nBiotic is a nonprofit research organization dedicated to the safe, responsible advancement of synthetic cell development. By supporting scientists at the forefront of bioengineering, we develop scalable solutions to mitigate global resource challenges well before we reach the critical threshold of 2050.\nRead mission statement\nRead mission statement\nApproach\nUnlocking transformative possibilities through foundational scientific discovery.  \nObligation\nOur goal is to deliver civilisational benefits for all people and the planet.\nPurpose\nWe are committed to building with transparency, public trust, and scientific rigor.\nThe evolution of biology\n\nBiotic builds and stewards the open, standardized foundations of biological engineering to accelerate discovery and ensure the benefits of biotechnology belong to everyone.\n\nLearn about SpudCell\nLearn about SpudCell\n\nRealizing the promise of synthetic cells requires a coordinated global effort across labs, nations, and disciplines. Guided by international collaboration, we publish research openly on this platform as it develops. The opportunities ahead are limitless.\n\nImagine:\nLifesaving medicines produced locally and on demand.\nA robust synthetic cell that can be programmed to make a protein where it is needed, and a protein-synthesis system twenty times more productive than today’s standards.\nCrops tailored precisely to their native soil and changing climates.\nAn operating system for designing multicellular biology at genome scale, so genomes can be modelled and corrected before ever built.\nCommunities monitoring their own water safety\nCell-free and synthetic cell based biosensing and manufacturing hardware small and simple enough to distribute\nHigh-performance building materials grown with zero environmental footprint.\nModules that let a cell make its own amino acids, nucleotides and energy, and an accounting system that maps the possibilities and morphologies those resources can afford.\nBiological compounds engineered to capture carbon and regenerate ecosystems.\nCells designed to run carbon-fixing pathways, the chemistry behind photosynthesis, so CO2 becomes a feedstock the cell builds from.\nJoin the community\nJoin the community\nBlog posts\nView all\nView all\n\nJuly 2, 2026\n\nOut of one, many.\nLearn more\nLearn more\nThe future of science starts now.\nFind out more\nFind out more\nGeneral inquiries\nhello@biotic.org\nJoin our mailing list\nLeave this field empty \nSign up\nSign up\nPalo Alto\n08:41am\nSan Diego\n08:41am\nMinneapolis\n10:41am\nMunich\n05:41pm\nPages\nMission\nResearch\nBlog\nAbout\nFollow\nLinkedIn\nX\nSubstack\nBluesky\nLegal\nPolicies & Procedures\nPrivacy\nTerms\nCookie Preferences\n8485:13:18:34\n©2026 Copyright Biotic\nBiotic is a U.S. 501(c)(3) nonprofit, non-stock organization\nDesign by Mucho. Build by Kaleido Grafik.\nImages created with RD tool by Karl Sims.",
