    "url": "https://exemplarfromsweden.com/",
    "finalUrl": "https://exemplarfromsweden.com/",
    "status": 200,
    "title": "Exemplar — A new typeface by Letters from Sweden",
    "text": "2026\nExemplar from Sweden\nMenu\nExemplar, SET IN STONE\nVIA CROCIALETTO, Pietrasanta\n32 years of work carved in marble\n\nA new typeface by Letters from Sweden\n\nExemplar has been drawn and redrawn for thirty years. To mark the final version, we carved its history into three street signs. One for each address and decade – where and when it took shape.\n\nExemplar now spans Latin, Cyrillic, Greek, and Arabic.\n\nIt is complete.\n\nWatch the film\n(1:28)\nExemplar Medium\n310pt\n\nMonument\n\nExemplar Medium\n334pt\n\nЭпитафия\n\nARTEMISGATAN, Hjorthagen\nA quiet street in a Stockholm suburb\nExemplar Medium\n323pt\n\nHoly Stone\n\nExemplar Medium\n328pt\n\nΠαρθενών\n\nVIA CROCIALETTO, Pietrasanta\nHands shaping letters\n\nIt doesn’t take three decades to design a typeface.\n\nBut, nonetheless, Göran began drawing what is now Exemplar, in 1994, on his Power Macintosh 7100.\n\nExemplar comes in 5 weights with italics, supporting 370 languages with its 1018 glyphs.\n\nWeight\nLight\nLight Italic\nRegular\nItalic\nMedium\nMedium Italic\nSemiBold\nSemiBold Italic\nBold\nBold Italic\nSize\npt\nStylistic Set\n2026\n2008\n1994\nArabic\nCyrillic\nLatin\nGreek\n\nTry for yourself\n\nSee all glyphs\nÅKERBÄRSVÄGEN, Torö\nLetters heading to Sweden\nLight\n\nWhat light is light, if Silvia be not seen? What joy is joy, if Silvia be not by? Unless it be to think that she is by, and feed upon the shadow of perfection.\n\nLight Italic\n\nIf music be the food of love, play on, give me excess of it; that surfeiting, the appetite may sicken, and so die. That strain again! it had a dying fall.\n\nRegular\n\nAll the world’s a stage, and all the men and women merely players; they have their exits and their entrances, and one man in his time plays many parts.\n\nRegular Italic\n\nWe are such stuff as dreams are made on, and our little life is rounded with a sleep. Sir, I am vexed; bear with my weakness; my old brain is troubled.\n\nMedium\n\nThe quality of mercy is not strained; it droppeth as the gentle rain from heaven upon the place beneath: it is twice blest; it blesseth him that gives and him that takes.\n\nMedium Italic\n\nSome are born great, some achieve greatness, and some have greatness thrust upon ‘em. Thy fates open their hands; let thy blood and spirit embrace them.\n\nSemiBold\n\nTo thine own self be true, and it must follow as the night the day, thou canst not then be false to any man. Farewell: my blessing season this in thee!\n\nSemiBold Italic\n\nThe robbed that smiles, steals something from the thief; he robs himself that spends a bootless grief. To mourn a mischief that is past and gone is the next way to draw new mischief on.\n\nBold\n\nWe few, we happy few, we band of brothers; for he today that sheds his blood with me shall be my brother; be he ne’er so vile, this day shall gentle his condition.\n\nBold Italic\n\nOut, out, brief candle! Life’s but a walking shadow, a poor player that struts and frets his hour upon the stage and then is heard no more.\n\nVIA CROCIALETTO, Pietrasanta\nTools for shaping stone\nExemplar Light with Flats\n264pt\n\nMultitudinous\n\nExemplar Arabic Regular\n214pt\n\nفي البدء كان الكلمة\n\nExemplar Light\n302pt\n\nPermanence\n\nExemplar Light\n325pt\n\nШановний\n\nSelect characters from Exemplar (2026)\n\nExemplar is not the work of a single mind. Nor a single set of hands. But it could not have existed without Göran. That much is true.\n\nA life’s work, made permanent at last.\n\n1994\n\n2026\n\nSTORY\nTYPEFACE\nSTONE\nHANDS\nBUY FONTS\nTHE END\nCopyright © 1994–2026\nLetters from Sweden\nWebsite by Here-Now",
